I’m Jinghui Lu, a Multimodal Algorithm Engineer currently working at ByteDance. I hold a Bachelor’s from Xiamen University’s School of Software and a Master’s and Ph.D. from University College Dublin’s School of Computer Science, advised by Professors Mark Keane and Brian Mac Namee. Previously, I was a Postdoctoral Researcher at the Insight Centre for Data Analytics and an AI Researcher at SenseTime. At Bytedance, my work is divided into two areas: half focuses on applied research, developing multimodal large models and large language models for advertising, particularly enhancing multimodal understanding for ad content like videos, images, and landing pages. The other half is dedicated to fundamental research, exploring topics far from business applications, such as multimodal model architectures, reinforcement learning, and reasoning in large language models. Over the past three years, I’ve published 13 papers at top conferences including AAAI, NeurIPS, ACL, ICCV, NAACL, and EMNLP, with 7 as first or co-first author.